# Line endings.
#
# Everything is stored in git with LF; that has always been true, but it was
# only ever true by accident of `core.autocrlf`. Stating it here means a clone
# on any machine agrees with CI.
#
# Go sources are checked out with LF as well, not just stored that way. gofmt
# treats CR as content, so a CRLF working tree makes `gofmt -l` name every file
# in the repository and the real offenders vanish into the noise. CI runs the
# same check on Linux, where the checkout is LF regardless — without this line
# the local check and the gate disagree.
* text=auto
*.go text eol=lf
*.png binary
